+"""Nessie (Capital One hackathon API) client: trip budget + savings tracker.
+
+How it works:
+  1. The user types a trip budget (e.g. $1,500).
+  2. create_trip() opens two fake Nessie accounts:
+       - "Trip Budget" (checking) holding the budget
+       - "Trip Savings" (savings) starting at $0
+  3. Every option the user picks (flight, hotel, food, activity) is a Nessie *purchase*
+     on Trip Budget. If the pick is cheaper than the typical option, the difference is
+     a Nessie *deposit* into Trip Savings, so savings show up as a real balance.
+  4. get_summary() returns budget / spent / saved / remaining / final trip total + every pick.
+
+Nessie is a sandbox: no real banks or money are involved. Docs: https://nessieisreal.com
+In demo mode (or with no NESSIE_API_KEY) everything runs against an in-memory fake.
